    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d930">

                <pb facs="0951" n="863" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg863"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Russell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-04-20"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 105.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith six copies of the
                    protocol between the United States and Venezuela.</p>
                <p>You will advise the Venezuelan Government that the United States Government has
                    named as its commissioner Mr. William E. Bainbridge, and as its agent before the
                    commission Mr. Robert C. Morris; also that the United States Government has
                    presented the request on its part to the Queen of the Netherlands to name an
                    umpire, pursuant to the protocol.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
